WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.627
Let’s summarize a small set of scores.

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:05.602
The mean gives the arithmetic average.

00:00:05.602 --> 00:00:09.517
The median gives the middle value after ordering the data.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:15.482
Minimum and maximum define the observed range, while standard deviation describes how spread out the values are around

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.706
the mean.

00:00:18.156 --> 00:00:21.083
No single statistic tells the whole story.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:29.913
Mean and median can respond differently to extreme values, and spread matters even when two datasets have the same

00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:36.950
average. Run the cell, then change one score to an extreme value and see which statistics move the most.
